Run in Linux/powershell terminal:
>gcc code.c -o code
>./code addresses.txt

Diverting output to output.txt:
>./code addresses.txt > output.txt

Run in Command Prompt:
>gcc code.c -o code
>code addresses.txt

Output redirection in CMD:
>code addresses.txt > output.txt

NOTE: When opening the output.txt file in VS-code refresh the encoding if random characters like (獹捩污愠摤敲獳›㠲㌰) appear or open the output.txt file in notepad. writing from PWSH creates a UTF-16LE encoded file whereas CMD and WSL create a UTF-8 file.

Recommended Terminal/Shell : PowerShell.